{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/882675-4th-eddition-better-one-world-system","id":882675,"title":"4th eddition: better one-world system.","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-05-05T01:30:27-07:00","id":882675,"title":"4th eddition: better one-world system.","content":"This isn't a cause for ballance. I'm not saying neonates should be on the same level as claith and that elder changelings should be as powerful as cathayans of the same age. Nor should the 4th dot of a mage sphere be equal to the 4th dot of a changeling cantrip. Nor do hunters with numina and formori... <br /> <br /> I could go on. Point is that the world of darkness is inherently not fair. But I think mechanics are strongly lacking in some areas, and it'd be nice if we got a better picture of some areas. <br /> <br /> <br /> I think the greatest lack in mechanics is of course powers with 'Difficulty=Stats they don't have'. We could go with the werewolf gift <i>Mothers touch</i> and how to heal someone, the difficulty is the target's rage, or five if they don't have rage. Or the gift Loki's touch where the difficulty is Rage+rank. Vampires fair somewhat better with Virtue+attribute (Since yeah, you could haphazardly assume someone's virtues through their rollplaying if you don't have them on a character sheet) But Ultimately I see this as a big problem.<br /> <br /> Secondly, well, some books imply more predators than others. Vampires in the VTM perspective know of werewolves,cathayans,changelings,mages,hunters and wraiths. That's really it if we don't count mummies, they're all wisely avoided.<br /> Now werewolf, on the otherhand, has all that, plus spirits which, to be fair, is a thing vampires are practically blind to, and then formori and pentex which some vampires work with. <br /> We go to mage and there's more nephandi and mauraders and the technocracy which totaly helps with the masquerade and their amazing clones and HIT marks which have found themselves in the hands of vampires and pentex... <br /> <br /> <br /> Now, It tends to be that vampire is first and everything's just added on to vampire/what came between. See the thing is that this keeps resetting so we've not really got a cool vampire setting with HIT marks and formori and Nephandi and the like.<br /> <br /> I'm still trying to struggle with what's in the sewers to be honest. With vampire; Just the nosferatu (and the niktuku hunting them, maybe tzmisce and an odd alligator) With werewolf it's the nosferatu, The ratkin, the Freakfeat, a few Gnawers... Really wondering how anything gets done down there. <br /> &quot;Tony, you ghouled the wrong rat for the last time&quot; <br /> *backstab*<br /> <br /> I'm not wanting anything equal or fair, I just want a clear modus operandi for playing all the games together. Nobody should give me weird looks when my Vampire tells the fianna, through medium of sluagh whom I communicate with through wraith intermediaries, of a mage plot that'll topple the environmentally friendly green government in the area, which will ultimately cause a fianna blood bath and allow me to get in and steal myself the magickal laser guns required to kill the nexus crawler i left within on of my ghouls after I thought I'd need a mighty formor to defend me against the might of stygia, who as you all know are quite pissed at me for using wraiths as emissaries to the unseelie.<br /> <br /> Alright, that's a joke. a massive mess. but, y'know, some books imply a mess. It really seems like we've got too many supernaturals sometimes and everywhere is something's territory. Unless it's vampire where you know Lupines stay out of the cities, Mages stay hidden, faeries are at best curiosities, advanced tech isn't really there and formori don't exist. I like that vampire focuses on itself, The courtly and inner struggles are a good place to focus; but there are way too many assets to take advantage of if you look out a bit, and every other line implies that vampires are in on their protagonist's problems. <br /> <br /> Using a HIT mark rather than a ghoul seems a bit more ethical. Making deals with pentex to get rid of the lupine menace seems like an ok idea. Finding out what owns the sewers seems like a solid plan. Having a mage hook you up with stuff is quite excellent. Having a vampire clean up it's businesses it owns in return for attacks on his rival seems like a good idea (not that garou were ever fond of those). <br /> <br /> As an added note- Mage was really more fun with it's whole huge, expanded weapon list. My friend was telling me I can't have a .50 anti-material rifle in vampire because the game Wasn't designed for that, even when I pointed to mage and said it's got a .50 weapon in it's rules. I really wanted a 5th gen dead, a .50 is big enough to justify lethal werever it hits and does more damage than silly-elder levels of stamina and fortitude can reliably deal with; and I like the tech advantage neonates have. But, some people are stingy. I liked Mage's approach. 20mm anti material rifle. <br /> <br /> TL;DR/Recap<br /> -Don't ballance supernaturals against supernaturals. Garou were meant to be stronger, Fae meant to be weaker..<br /> -Do put in new systems for when not using a power against the same kind (IE don't ask for a Kindred's Rage+Rank). Werewolf is a pretty terrible defender for this. Also don't do 'extra Dice is equal to valor' cause guys outside that renown system end up confused. Also don't claim damage unsoakable when it could be soaked by other supernaturals. <br /> - Explain the contested areas in a way that makes sociological,political... Whatever sense. How are the sewers shared? How much do secret organisations know/deal with secret organisations (ok, that one sounds like a WoD general book) How do the fleabags react when a cainite walks through a bonegnawer sept? What happens when X tries to takeover a company owned by Ventrue, Glass walkers, Pentex, Yeren, The Technocracy (or traditions) A sidhe (do Changelings do that?) or just humans that are damn wary about the shit they know some freaks pull. I mean multi-million dollar companies are a highly contested resource and I'm sure each group encounters things which shouldn't be when they compete for them. <br /> - I'm not asking for vampire to have the whole of every other book inside of it. <br /> <br /> Or maybe I'm asking for a generic Classic world of darkness 4th edition book to lay the groundwork.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7244-innocent-flower","name":"Innocent Flower","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7244_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"322"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-05T05:36:22-07:00","id":882791,"title":"","content":"Considering what we've seen in the BNS Werewolf Delta Slice you'll probably have your wish. Martin has talked a lot about the One World of Darkness and how they are going to build it up from the bottom up so it works all together. Sadly, for me that will probably be the day when I stop supporting this gameline and invest into other things that actually interest me.<br /> <br /> The WoD as a completely interconnected and well reasoned whole is a pipe dream. The games themselves pretty much trample the basic societal and environmental constraints between them. Each of the games actually focuses on what matters for itself, and the other critters and their idiosyncracies are not it. I do not want a Mage or Werewolf game where i have to worry about the Masquerade, Antedelluvians ot the Hieararchy. Anytime another critter shows up it's supposed to be strange, exotic and understood within the terms of the game you're playing, not a mythical perfectly interconnected world.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-05T08:56:04-07:00","id":882904,"title":"","content":"I think a one-world book is something storytellers should have. Not players. <br /> <br /> (but working out difficulties on a target's rage and rank, which nobody really has, really needs to go. Werewolf is so bad for this kind of stuff)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7244-innocent-flower","name":"Innocent Flower","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7244_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"322"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-05T09:19:52-07:00","id":882918,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Innocent Flower</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/882675-4th-eddition-better-one-world-system?p=882904#post882904\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think a one-world book is something storytellers should have. Not players. <br /> <br /> (but working out difficulties on a target's rage and rank, which nobody really has, really needs to go. Werewolf is so bad for this kind of stuff)</div> </div> </div> </div>Same with basing difficulties on humanity/path.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3075-coridan","name":"Coridan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3075_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"528"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-05T12:45:14-07:00","id":883121,"title":"","content":"While I'm not agreeing with everything in the OP's post, I realy hope the guys and girls in WW will work out the One WoD fine. While I understand and agree with the opinion that the gamelines should focus on their own thing, BUT for me that doesn't mean they should be exclusive. In my head the WoD was always One Wod where the different factions and critters exist along (they are in each other's core books, they know about each other, in cases, they have serious history, like the Tremere), and honestly for me crossover is not a bad thing. If the new edition actualy makes the rules more compatible among the lines and makes the world a little more logicaly comprehensive (however I never get this whole absolute heresy attitude toward a shared setting and crossover so far), well, all the good for me! Sincerely, I think the X20 lines already have this attitude, more or less, albeit not rules-wise in the most part, and I'm glad for it.<br /> <br /> In short, I think if we get the potential to play, for example Vampire, with a strong focus on Vampire's things and leave the others largely out of the picture if we want, but also get the chance to mingle the lines in a more comprehensive way setting and rules-wise, I'd be glad. I'm absolutely on the side of more feasibility against exclusiveness and anything compulsory.<br /> <br /> Don't get me worng, I have fears about the new edition, I found some of ME's statements concerning. I'm not sure at all the new edition'd be for me and in that case I'd be sad. It's totaly possibble that they'd make the One WoD or any of the lines in a way that wouldn't appeal to me, story-wise, aestheticaly or in tone. In that case I'll have the X20s fortunately! But I give them the chance and the plan to make the WoD one comprehensive world in on itself is a definitely plus in my book so far.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>If nothing worked, then let's think!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6363-pm\u00e1rk","name":"PM\u00e1rk","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6363_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2363"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-05T13:28:06-07:00","id":883169,"title":"","content":"I find it rather ironic that the press statement by Martin started condemning Exalted right out of the gate for having even the most tangential relation to a WoD as a whole (was this more prominent in LARP? It's never been more than a few wink wink nudge nudge references in tabletop), yet Exalted actually manages to blend all of the basic themes of the WoD together into a mostly cohesive whole, if in a totally different genre.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-06T04:48:18-07:00","id":883649,"title":"","content":"One World of Darkness does a disservice to every single individual gameline. If you're going to have a unified, coherent setting with Vampires, Werewolves, Wraiths, Mages, Fae and the kitchen sink, you have to write it as such from the beginning and not under the assumption that it's supposed to be usable for games that are specifically and exclusively about Mages and Mage business. (or whichever gameline.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2082-schleiermacher","name":"Schleiermacher","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"190"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-06T06:49:13-07:00","id":883706,"title":"","content":"I feel the same way for the most part... but.. should Garou have the same option of &quot;Cannibalizing Tempers&quot; that changelings have.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-06T09:51:05-07:00","id":883860,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Coridan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/882675-4th-eddition-better-one-world-system?p=882918#post882918\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Same with basing difficulties on humanity/path.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I think rage/gnosis/specific supernatural energy is worse for it. You could really guess humanity and virtues for anything, since they're there for almost everything even if a werewolf wouldn't have a stat for his conscience or a sidhe wouldn't consider how not-psycho he is on a scale of 1-10. Meanwhile difficulty of the targets rage, or 5 if they have none... yeah that's to simplistic. Nobody has rage but thematically I'm struggling to see how a Methusela is just as vulnerable to that as a neonate is.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7244-innocent-flower","name":"Innocent Flower","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7244_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"322"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-06T13:29:31-07:00","id":884024,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Innocent Flower</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/882675-4th-eddition-better-one-world-system?p=883860#post883860\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> I think rage/gnosis/specific supernatural energy is worse for it. You could really guess humanity and virtues for anything, since they're there for almost everything even if a werewolf wouldn't have a stat for his conscience or a sidhe wouldn't consider how not-psycho he is on a scale of 1-10. Meanwhile difficulty of the targets rage, or 5 if they have none... yeah that's to simplistic. Nobody has rage but thematically I'm struggling to see how a Methusela is just as vulnerable to that as a neonate is.</div> </div> </div> </div>Mother's Touch is a healing Gift that explicitly doesn't heal the undead, so I'd ask vulnerable to what exactly, but there's also the importance of spiritual connections to consider in Werewolf. Vampires are outright dead inside, so there's that; there's no guarantee of having high Virtues when you've spent centuries or millennia working to steadily erode them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-06T14:51:40-07:00","id":884094,"title":"","content":"It's not just mothers touch that's difficulty of the target's rage. Many gifts/charms are contested against rage, gnosis and rank. Whilst you're sounding like I should say 'Vampires are spiritually dead, that gift (likely offensive in nature) just doesn't work on them.&quot; I do also put forth mages. &quot;Difficulty of Arete&quot; or &quot;Difficulty of Target's quintessence&quot; is... Well, I suppose avatar+Arete is almost as good as Rage+rank, but it's still a mess.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7244-innocent-flower","name":"Innocent Flower","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7244_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"322"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-06T15:13:16-07:00","id":884110,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Innocent Flower</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/882675-4th-eddition-better-one-world-system?p=884094#post884094\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's not just mothers touch that's difficulty of the target's rage. Many gifts/charms are contested against rage, gnosis and rank. Whilst you're sounding like I should say 'Vampires are spiritually dead, that gift (likely offensive in nature) just doesn't work on them.&quot; I do also put forth mages. &quot;Difficulty of Arete&quot; or &quot;Difficulty of Target's quintessence&quot; is... Well, I suppose avatar+Arete is almost as good as Rage+rank, but it's still a mess.</div> </div> </div> </div>Just so long as Rank isn't used as a stand-in for Generation. That's always been a terrible choice.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-06T17:02:35-07:00","id":884163,"title":"","content":"Imo if you put in a One WoD setting you have to balance a lot of stuff because if you don't you screw the PC at the table, that are playing the weaker parts and for me I never really liked crossovers or using a different splat book for NPC. 1st it's to predictable and 2nd you can completely negate some important parts of the canon. I.e. Tremere wouldn't make no sense if there are some super warping mages all round the globe fighting an ascension war. Because why give up that kind of power because of a little fluctuations in mana for brief time, yeah totally makes sense. <br /> I think after VTM another bunch of authors said to them self, well lets create something that could f**k'em all to death and that creation was called werewolf. Then repeating the cycle and thus Mage was created. <br /> <br /> But thats not the worst of all, the lore on all splats is completely contrary to each other, and I think they will disappoint a lot of people when the sort that mess out, because they can't be all right.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5970-meldok","name":"Meldok","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"221"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-06T17:33:36-07:00","id":884177,"title":"","content":"From the time VtM first came out and all the other games were add. All the STs in the area I was playing in used them as just addons to VtM. Everyone played each of the different game(Vtm,WtA,MtA,etc.) using what ever core book for the game they were running. If they needed to introduce another splat, they would use it's core book if they had it or the write up in the game they were running if they didn't. Everyone in the gaming community viewed it as one world, just with different core books based upon what you wanted to play. Everyone assumed that the game (WoD) was written so that if you just wanted to play vampire you only had to buy the vampire books, but the publishers expected the players to buy everything as it came out. Which is what most of our gamers did. I myself ended up with all the vampire books, about 90% of the werewolf books, 75% of the mage books, 40% of the changeling books and about 20% of the wraith books, before they ended the original line.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Reboot","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3684-david-g","name":"David G","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3684_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"176"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-09T15:15:25-07:00","id":886665,"title":"","content":"The biggest problem with a single cosmology is, where do you start? Do you start with the Judeo-Christian cosmology of Demon the Fallen and Vampire and say that that cosmology is correct and werewolves (and others) are deluded and misunderstand what is going on? Do you do the opposite and start from the Werewold/Mage view with a sort of Triat? Whichever is chosen, it is going to alienate a large swath of players as their game is now objectively wrong.<br /> <br /> The World of Darkness is meant to be integrated to a degree, but I think having a single cosmology is a bad idea. It was one of the worst sins Demon the Fallen did, trying to absorb other games cosmology into itself, effectively saying the members of those gamelines (werewolves, kuei-jin, mummies, etc) were objectively wrong and the major figures of their cosmologies (Gaia, the Triat, the Ebony Dragon, etc) were just angels and such.<br /> <br /> Still, it wasn't that bad since Demon the Fallen was it's own game and had its own cosmology and it didn't interfere with the other games. The books never actuallt said, &quot;these guys are right,&quot; even if it did heavily imply it. But with a &quot;one world of darkness &quot; that likely won't still be the case and we'll have one cosmology to rule them all.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":741,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","user":"AnubisXy","date":". 05-09-2016, 06:17 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-09T15:29:50-07:00","id":886674,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AnubisXy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/882675-4th-eddition-better-one-world-system?p=886665#post886665\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The biggest problem with a single cosmology is, where do you start? Do you start with the Judeo-Christian cosmology of Demon the Fallen and Vampire and say that that cosmology is correct and werewolves (and others) are deluded and misunderstand what is going on? Do you do the opposite and start from the Werewold/Mage view with a sort of Triat? Whichever is chosen, it is going to alienate a large swath of players as their game is now objectively wrong.<br /> <br /> The World of Darkness is meant to be integrated to a degree, but I think having a single cosmology is a bad idea. It was one of the worst sins Demon the Fallen did, trying to absorb other games cosmology into itself, effectively saying the members of those gamelines (werewolves, kuei-jin, mummies, etc) were objectively wrong and the major figures of their cosmologies (Gaia, the Triat, the Ebony Dragon, etc) were just angels and such.<br /> <br /> Still, it wasn't that bad since Demon the Fallen was it's own game and had its own cosmology and it didn't interfere with the other games. The books never actuallt said, &quot;these guys are right,&quot; even if it did heavily imply it. But with a &quot;one world of darkness &quot; that likely won't still be the case and we'll have one cosmology to rule them all.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yet, it was bad, because even more people from the D:tF corner take it to be the true case to apply to everything else. Then they go around in circles talking about &quot;layered reality&quot; like it actually means something.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-09T19:10:16-07:00","id":886857,"title":"","content":"Relatively few people are asking for a unified cosmology though, as that really isn't necessary. Cosmology works as backstory/setting fluff, but as far as game is concerned it's mostly meaningless for the here and now. The origin of vampires for instance is largely irrelevant to most vampire games and would likely be even less relevant in games that feature heavy cross-over. The bigger question is how to deal with abilities that work on different rule sets (e.g. difficulties based on Humanity, virtues, Rank, renown, etcetera) or abilities that other creatures can't do fuck all about, i.e. with earlier versions of Turn Vampire into Lawn Chair and other similar ritual spells, there was basically nothing a non-mage could do. There are acceptable differences in power but then there is just being blatantly unfair.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1136-wolfgar","name":"Wolfgar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1136_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"646"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-09T19:38:09-07:00","id":886883,"title":"","content":"I don't really see why One WoD is such a bad thing. If you don't want your vampire/werewolf/whatever game to include parts of the world that are generally thought of as part of a different splat then noone is stopping you from simply disregarding those aspects, think lupines in vampire.<br /> <br /> But for those of us that want it to be one cohesive world where everything has clear rules for interactions between splats this might be great. It remains to be seen.<br /> <br /> Also regarding the cosmology, there doesn't need to be one version that is objectively true.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4003-kristviljan","name":"Kristviljan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4003_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"110"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-10T07:06:22-07:00","id":887136,"title":"","content":"I agree in that a more cohesive ruling doesn't necesarily have to mess with cosmological issues. God(s) are misterious and all that...<br /> <br /> The triky part would be to make sense of the aspects of the history/metaplot that are closer to the daily lives of our heros. Like how it's possible that both the Camarilla and the Technocracy, having the sort of power that they have, somehow know nearly nothing about each other. Or how it's that the Technocrats can have a straight face when priorizing Traditionalist hippies over Sabbat vampires as &quot;a treat to humanity&quot;...Yeah, I know everyone has a headcanon explanation about that, it's not impossible to do, but it's triky to do without doing a disservice to some or other game.<br /> <br /> Another triky part would be doing rules that aren't &quot;Vampires rules, everyone else's powers fail&quot; <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> . I've seen far to many times in Mage rules that exist solely so vampires can survive against True Magick. Rules that are horrible both from a cosmological point of view (giving vampires methapisical privileges, like making sunlight Forces 5 + Spirit 5 + Prime 4, or some other ludicrously high Spheres) and from a practical point of view (Mage it's all about finding holes in the rules, not a single rule made to &quot;protect vampires&quot; has ever worked for anything but to frustrate players and storytellers).<br /> <br /> And besides, really, do vampires and others need that sort of protection?, because they never seemed that weak to me.I think that people merely underestimates vampires or overestimates mages. For instance, the aforementioned Lawnchair ritual. It was easy enough to just kill the mage casting the ritual, to do said ritual from a safe distance you needed mastery over Correspondence, not only Life (and Mastery it's hard to get. Level 5 Spheres shouldn't be compared with level 5 Disciplines, Spheres are rarer and more difficult to get, not to mention the methapisical differences).<br /> Even before the new rules, the real problem wasn't the ritual itself, but the fact that a mage with Correspondence can do it from anywhere. Taumaturges/other &quot;mages&quot; need a reliable (not easy, reliable) way to unweave magical rituals, or to protect against ranged magic, not some wierd &quot;vampiric immunities&quot; (that, ironically, work better against instant magic than against ritual magic).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-10T07:28:46-07:00","id":887146,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kristviljan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/882675-4th-eddition-better-one-world-system?p=886883#post886883\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't really see why One WoD is such a bad thing. If you don't want your vampire/werewolf/whatever game to include parts of the world that are generally thought of as part of a different splat then noone is stopping you from simply disregarding those aspects, think lupines in vampire.<br /> <br /> But for those of us that want it to be one cohesive world where everything has clear rules for interactions between splats this might be great. It remains to be seen.<br /> <br /> Also regarding the cosmology, there doesn't need to be one version that is objectively true.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, even if all that is still in place from where it is now... I liked the metaplot in Werewolf because it had an extremely light touch, like the projection of events regarding the Yugashi invasion of the South in Exalted's Time of Tumult. The events were there for groups to use in campaigns, not sweep you away. If they're going to be doing wider-scale metaplots in a single world, things can get in the faces of everyone very quickly, and in a very bad way.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-11T06:08:36-07:00","id":888099,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aleph</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/882675-4th-eddition-better-one-world-system?p=887136#post887136\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Another triky part would be doing rules that aren't &quot;Vampires rules, everyone else's powers fail&quot; <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> . I've seen far to many times in Mage rules that exist solely so vampires can survive against True Magick. Rules that are horrible both from a cosmological point of view (giving vampires methapisical privileges, like making sunlight Forces 5 + Spirit 5 + Prime 4, or some other ludicrously high Spheres) and from a practical point of view (Mage it's all about finding holes in the rules, not a single rule made to &quot;protect vampires&quot; has ever worked for anything but to frustrate players and storytellers).<br /> <br /> And besides, really, do vampires and others need that sort of protection?, because they never seemed that weak to me.I think that people merely underestimates vampires or overestimates mages.</div> </div> </div> </div>I just going to flatly disagree with you there. In every crossover game I've ever played in over twelve years and multiple groups across multiple states there are Mage players and STs who will go out of their way to whip out their dicks and piss on vampires for no other reason than the lulz. You may say that this is a problem with individuals, and to an extent I agree. However this sort of attitude has until recently been reinforced by the setting. The general stance of writers for much of the CWoD was &quot;Mages Win. The End.&quot; Probably no better example of this exists than one of the apocalyptic setting fixtures of Vampire getting casually rubbed out from space by a Technocrat desk jockey pushing a button.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2507-caitiff-primogen","name":"Caitiff Primogen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2507_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1351"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-11T07:58:21-07:00","id":888202,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Caitiff Primogen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/882675-4th-eddition-better-one-world-system?p=888099#post888099\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I just going to flatly disagree with you there. In every crossover game I've ever played in over twelve years and multiple groups across multiple states there are Mage players and STs who will go out of their way to whip out their dicks and piss on vampires for no other reason than the lulz. You may say that this is a problem with individuals, and to an extent I agree. However this sort of attitude has until recently been reinforced by the setting. The general stance of writers for much of the CWoD was &quot;Mages Win. The End.&quot; Probably no better example of this exists than one of the apocalyptic setting fixtures of Vampire getting casually rubbed out from space by a Technocrat desk jockey pushing a button.</div> </div> </div> </div>While I can definitely sympathize with this in some respects, killing Zapathasura was presented as an effort that overextended the resources of the Union. The major casualties were really the Hungry Dead, anyway, since the spirit nukes that hit first killed all three of them right out but may or may not have done anything to Zapathasura.<br /> <br /> Getting back to handling Mage, though, the problems will probably remain for as long as the splat does. Vampires have a number of effects for which they can use blood without getting Disciplines, turning into other forms doesn't require a Garou or Fera to learn other Gifts, wraiths are outright ghosts, changelings are fae creatures, and even the Imbued are a kind of anti-monster in this regard with an inherent ability to confront other monsters without being shut down immediately, but mages are presented as being far too human, with the &quot;balance&quot; being that their powers are more powerful. I don't think that this was a good balance point, or a setting feature. The otherness of Avatars really needs to be emphasized, along with some kind of strange inherent power that doesn't rely on Spheres, but it doesn't end there by any means, of course.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-11T08:52:49-07:00","id":888251,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/882675-4th-eddition-better-one-world-system?p=888202#post888202\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> While I can definitely sympathize with this in some respects, killing Zapathasura was presented as an effort that overextended the resources of the Union. The major casualties were really the Hungry Dead, anyway, since the spirit nukes that hit first killed all three of them right out but may or may not have done anything to Zapathasura.<br /> <br /> Getting back to handling Mage, though, the problems will probably remain for as long as the splat does. Vampires have a number of effects for which they can use blood without getting Disciplines, turning into other forms doesn't require a Garou or Fera to learn other Gifts, wraiths are outright ghosts, changelings are fae creatures, and even the Imbued are a kind of anti-monster in this regard with an inherent ability to confront other monsters without being shut down immediately, but mages are presented as being far too human, with the &quot;balance&quot; being that their powers are more powerful. I don't think that this was a good balance point, or a setting feature. The otherness of Avatars really needs to be emphasized, along with some kind of strange inherent power that doesn't rely on Spheres, but it doesn't end there by any means, of course.</div> </div> </div> </div>Casualties, or lack thereof, is kind of my problem with that whole situation. If they'd at least had an Ante-freaking-diluvian take some Technocrats with him it would have removed some of the sting. The impression it gives though is of an entirely remote operation. They might as well have farted him to death from the safety of orbit. It doesn't really matter how hard or tiring that fart was, without any sort of real human cost there was no point to it.<br /> <br /> Honestly I'd totally be in favor of giving Mages some more innate benefits in exchange for reigning in the power of Spheres a bit. Their supposed mortality pretty much goes out the window around the time they hit Arete 3 and by then there's precious little that ever seems to slow their roll.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2507-caitiff-primogen","name":"Caitiff Primogen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2507_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1351"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-11T09:25:04-07:00","id":888280,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aleph</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/882675-4th-eddition-better-one-world-system?p=887136#post887136\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Even before the new rules, the real problem wasn't the ritual itself, but the fact that a mage with Correspondence can do it from anywhere. Taumaturges/other &quot;mages&quot; need a reliable (not easy, reliable) way to unweave magical rituals, or to protect against ranged magic, not some wierd &quot;vampiric immunities&quot; (that, ironically, work better against instant magic than against ritual magic).</div> </div> </div> </div>I agree that this might be an overall better way to handle it, although limiting it solely to the purview of Thamaturges only further advantages an already broken aspect of Vampire, which is its own separate can of worms.<br /> <br /> The other big problem is that the relative strength of the target doesn't really matter. With the same spell cast by the same Mage you can point at a thin-blooded neonate and say &quot;Poof! Lawnchair!&quot; then turn around and point at a methuselah older than agriculture and say &quot;Poof! Fuckin' Lawnchair!&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2507-caitiff-primogen","name":"Caitiff Primogen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2507_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1351"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-11T14:58:42-07:00","id":888584,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Caitiff Primogen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/882675-4th-eddition-better-one-world-system?p=888251#post888251\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Casualties, or lack thereof, is kind of my problem with that whole situation. If they'd at least had an Ante-freaking-diluvian take some Technocrats with him it would have removed some of the sting. The impression it gives though is of an entirely remote operation. They might as well have farted him to death from the safety of orbit. It doesn't really matter how hard or tiring that fart was, without any sort of real human cost there was no point to it.<br /> <br /> Honestly I'd totally be in favor of giving Mages some more innate benefits in exchange for reigning in the power of Spheres a bit. Their supposed mortality pretty much goes out the window around the time they hit Arete 3 and by then there's precious little that ever seems to slow their roll.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well to put you at least at ease a bit, the Techies did send multiple military units in there, which probably included badass frontline techs to deal with this shit. What freaked them out and triggered the Ragnarok protocol was that they lost comms with their best people in the field and the mayhem and rampant eschatonism was getting worse and worse.<br /> <br /> Funnily, the spheres are quite reigned in, due to the way that Disciplines above 5 pretty much autowin against spheres, and that there is a million subrules to make it harder and more costly in XP for Mages to actually touch vampires. The whole lawnchair thing is completley blown out of proportion, as it needs a paradigm that supports is (which most of them don't), a shitload of preparation worthy of a whole storyline, a ton of quintessence to keep the rite going and is more likely to kill the mage trying it (because he will probably botch it) then to actually work properly.<br /> <br /> The Mage has an edge if he knows the vampire well (how, and why doesn't the vampire know it?), if he is far far away (which the vampire shouldn't be allowing since he knows that only good threat is a dead threat) and has a lot of time to cast a bombastic ritual to simply torch his haven to the ground with a conveniently placed destructive effect (and yes, it will be a indirect destructive effect since those are actually straightforward compared to mind control and changing the other's body).<br /> <br /> Frankly it's a dick measuring contest and not worth you while. If you're running vampire, mages are neither omnipotent nor particularly important to the plot. The same applies for every other game line.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-11T15:45:38-07:00","id":888627,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Asmodai</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/882675-4th-eddition-better-one-world-system?p=888584#post888584\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Well to put you at least at ease a bit, the Techies did send multiple military units in there, which probably included badass frontline techs to deal with this shit. What freaked them out and triggered the Ragnarok protocol was that they lost comms with their best people in the field and the mayhem and rampant eschatonism was getting worse and worse.<br /> <br /> Funnily, the spheres are quite reigned in, due to the way that Disciplines above 5 pretty much autowin against spheres, and that there is a million subrules to make it harder and more costly in XP for Mages to actually touch vampires. The whole lawnchair thing is completley blown out of proportion, as it needs a paradigm that supports is (which most of them don't), a shitload of preparation worthy of a whole storyline, a ton of quintessence to keep the rite going and is more likely to kill the mage trying it (because he will probably botch it) then to actually work properly.<br /> <br /> The Mage has an edge if he knows the vampire well (how, and why doesn't the vampire know it?), if he is far far away (which the vampire shouldn't be allowing since he knows that only good threat is a dead threat) and has a lot of time to cast a bombastic ritual to simply torch his haven to the ground with a conveniently placed destructive effect (and yes, it will be a indirect destructive effect since those are actually straightforward compared to mind control and changing the other's body).<br /> <br /> Frankly it's a dick measuring contest and not worth you while. If you're running vampire, mages are neither omnipotent nor particularly important to the plot. The same applies for every other game line.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, just as with not using Rank of Gift level as Discipline level, hopefully any system that follows doesn't use Sphere level for Discipline level, either. Or Arts, or Arcanoi, etc. They just aren't meant to scale like Disciplines are, and the other games shouldn't be shoved aside because they dared to not have a strict hierarchy of power in some fashion.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-11T17:35:56-07:00","id":888689,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Caitiff Primogen</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">I just going to flatly disagree with you there. In every crossover game I've ever played in over twelve years and multiple groups across multiple states there are Mage players and STs who will go out of their way to whip out their dicks and piss on vampires for no other reason than the lulz. You may say that this is a problem with individuals, and to an extent I agree. However this sort of attitude has until recently been reinforced by the setting. The general stance of writers for much of the CWoD was &quot;Mages Win. The End.&quot; Probably no better example of this exists than one of the apocalyptic setting fixtures of Vampire getting casually rubbed out from space by a Technocrat desk jockey pushing a button.</div> </div> </div> </div>Maybe that's so in the metaplot (magic, of every kind, was always used by WW as Deus Ex Machina for everything), but regarding rules...<br /> <br /> In Mage, rules always were bent (in weird and ineficient ways) towards vampires.<br /> <br /> For instance: Did you know that the (quite ignored) rule to Evade Magic was originaly invented to protect Mathusaleas so they can evade the &quot;lawnchair&quot; rote and similars? It's true, if you go to the Book of Shadows (Mage 1rst ed), it's stated in such a way. <i>Man, that Rote surely had a backlash...</i><br /> <br /> That was the first attempt at a defense for vampires (useful for others but never stated in such a way).<br /> <br /> In the newer rules, Supernaturals get a +3 to difficulty of Mind magick, +5 if they have Dominate (no other mental power gets mentioned, not even Mind magick). Stated to be so you can't use Mind on a vampire in HDYDT.<br /> <br /> Guess how easy it's to Dominate (or use any other Discipline, realy) an Archmage. As difficult any mortal, unless they have a Mind shield, and that doesn't work unless the Mage has a greater level in Mind than the vampire in Dominate (way too dificult, if we ponder the rarity of level 5 Spheres, and the fact that not all Archmages are Masters of Mind). You have other rules, but Discipline vs Power it's the most common, and other splats also suffer because of the fact that Disciplines just have more levels (not that they're stronger in any way, they just have more levels) than their powers.<br /> <br /> Then let's go to Hunter. They're inmune to ALL mental powers and illusions, but a supernatural with 6+ on a power may get a chance at bypassing it to represent a trully exeptional power. Guess what splat it's characterized for having powers over 6. Vampires (and, maybe, Mages. Granted that with what Mages can do to Hunters by using Prime, they have nothing to complain about.)<br /> <br /> Also, I see a certain level 6 Gift on Werewolf that had a very low, almost nonexistant, but very real chance of actualy working against Mathusaleas and even Antediluvians, that got retconned in W20 so it can't possibly affect trully elder vampires...Was it necessary to nerf it?, Aren't Rank 6 the closest thing to an Elder Level that Werewolves have?.<br /> <br /> Also, why Mathusaleas always need to be the strongest boys arround? . It's not like they will appear in front of an altar as some kind of &quot;final boss&quot; in a Crossover chronicle <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/confused.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Confused\" smilieid=\"10\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <i>'Cause if you stay away and attack by surprise with minions while hiding your name/identity you don't need to worry about the &quot;lawnchair rote&quot;.</i> But OF COURSE, Mathusaleas NEVER do that, they go <i>Incredible Hulk style </i>against the characters, and<i> demand</i> said characters to be defensless against that &quot;strategy&quot;. When they aren't, it's obviously a problem of the rules.<br /> <i>(Trully, Ravnos just went on a rampage...that was his milenary plot? , his ageless prep for the Gehena? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/confused.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Confused\" smilieid=\"10\" class=\"inlineimg\" />)</i><br /> <br /> Now, that's not to say that there aren't things in Mage that are OP. The main problem comes from attacks that trully have no defense, like being teleported to a volcano/the sun/bottom of the ocean, or the &quot;time stop&quot;. And from info. gathering magicks that seem almost impossible to defend against.<br /> <br /> But the problem isn't that poor little Elders can't do anything against that (as stated, there are ways for the inteligent, and powerful Elders CAN have some custom Rituals/Disciplines that work against Magick. They were arround too much time to have no protection against such a direct threat), the problem it's that, sometimes, powers that you take for granted are going to be outclassed. This problem it's experimented by the players. It happens to the Akashick that has to keep up with the Brujah and to the evil plotter that has to keep up with info gathering magick. It's wierd (and needs handwaving) to storytell when your characters have absolutely no defense against what a given antagonist can do. That's why storyteller's mages rarely send you to a volcano. That's also why Werewolves tend to attack solo instead of going in packs <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> But I disgress...I think it's better to reign the differences by creating some degree of defense that can be used agains't others in certain cases than by nerfing everyone so everyone can fight with equal chance.<br /> It's OK if sometimes you get overpowered. In vampire it happens all the time, like when an elder targets you with Dominate, or when a Taumaturge casts a curse on you. That's why powers are scary, if everything can be countered, nothing it's trully scary while you have good dice on your hand.<br /> Also, sometimes, (when the power isn't completely broken) it can be fun to decipher how to counter a given power. If you can't pierce a Ward on a Chantry despite your Strength 16, don't complain against the rules, just throw something really heavy at the Chantry (preferably, something that explodes <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> ), chance it's that the Ward was designed agains't your splat, not against random things.<br /> <br /> If small discrepancies between games get balanced, the setting it's set so everyone can live in the same world without killing each other, and the rest it's treated on the basis that Powerfull characters can have powerful defenses/offenses, that no power it's infalible. That's everything that's trully needed.<br /> Oh, and this:<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, just as with not using Rank of Gift level as Discipline level, hopefully any system that follows doesn't use Sphere level for Discipline level, either. Or Arts, or Arcanoi, etc. They just aren't meant to scale like Disciplines are, and the other games shouldn't be shoved aside because they dared to not have a strict hierarchy of power in some fashion.</div> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1683,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","user":"Aleph","date":". 05-11-2016, 08:44 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-11T19:42:43-07:00","id":888777,"title":"","content":"Honestly while I was the one who brought up Methuselahs and Antediluvians I'm not really all that concerned about them in the grand scheme. Nobody likes NPC theater, so their susceptibility or not to awakened magic should really be mostly in the hands of STs and writers.<br /> <br /> My area of concern is PC level characters in PvP. Maybe it shouldn't happen, but it does happen and it's going to continue happening. Perfect white room balance is neither achievable nor desirable, but vampires are almost always relegated to the position of yardstick vis a vis the other splats. Now some of those rules you've mentioned I was legitimately unaware of. There is clearly already some text that has attempted to address this, however the fact that this is first time I'm hearing about it indicates that Mage players and STs with whom I have interacted were either themselves unaware of it or deliberately chose to ignore it, as they were never mentioned in any of the various rules discussions these situations created. If it were just one group where this had happened it would be one thing, but I'm speaking from direct experience with multiple samples over an extended period of time, which suggests broader trends in player behavior. That isn't really something that can be addressed in game text, but I'm going to continue to advocate for more inter-splat balance and fight efforts to erode what balance exists. I do apologize if any of this has come off as petulant, but this particular teeth grinder has been pissing me off for over a decade at this point and I've grown weary of being polite about it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2507-caitiff-primogen","name":"Caitiff Primogen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2507_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1351"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-12T02:42:29-07:00","id":888978,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Caitiff Primogen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/882675-4th-eddition-better-one-world-system?p=888777#post888777\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Honestly while I was the one who brought up Methuselahs and Antediluvians I'm not really all that concerned about them in the grand scheme. Nobody likes NPC theater, so their susceptibility or not to awakened magic should really be mostly in the hands of STs and writers.<br /> <br /> My area of concern is PC level characters in PvP. Maybe it shouldn't happen, but it does happen and it's going to continue happening. Perfect white room balance is neither achievable nor desirable, but vampires are almost always relegated to the position of yardstick vis a vis the other splats. Now some of those rules you've mentioned I was legitimately unaware of. There is clearly already some text that has attempted to address this, however the fact that this is first time I'm hearing about it indicates that Mage players and STs with whom I have interacted were either themselves unaware of it or deliberately chose to ignore it, as they were never mentioned in any of the various rules discussions these situations created. If it were just one group where this had happened it would be one thing, but I'm speaking from direct experience with multiple samples over an extended period of time, which suggests broader trends in player behavior. That isn't really something that can be addressed in game text, but I'm going to continue to advocate for more inter-splat balance and fight efforts to erode what balance exists. I do apologize if any of this has come off as petulant, but this particular teeth grinder has been pissing me off for over a decade at this point and I've grown weary of being polite about it.</div> </div> </div> </div>The problem is that very few people actually properly read everything and tend to be gameline partisans. This means that they will end up using each and every possible power and trick permutation they can think of without actually considering the context. Most discussions about who can do what and who will win why come down to someone whiterooming a set of complex issues to prove &quot;their&quot; guys are the best.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-12T06:30:17-07:00","id":889050,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Asmodai</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/882675-4th-eddition-better-one-world-system?p=888978#post888978\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The problem is that very few people actually properly read everything and tend to be gameline partisans. This means that they will end up using each and every possible power and trick permutation they can think of without actually considering the context. Most discussions about who can do what and who will win why come down to someone whiterooming a set of complex issues to prove &quot;their&quot; guys are the best.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is true, and to be fair it does cut Mages as well. They can only do as much as the STs let them do, and it always seems to fall out one of two ways. Either the ST is a Mage partisan and will give them carte blanche to get away with murder, or they are not and will tend to cut the Mages off at the knees. The first isn't fun for anyone not playing a Mage, and the latter isn't fun for anyone playing a Mage. There's really no winning.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2507-caitiff-primogen","name":"Caitiff Primogen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2507_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1351"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-12T07:31:27-07:00","id":889102,"title":"","content":"Mage it's a game where you really need to read all the rules. If you stay with what's written in the Spheres, without understanding the difficulty to pull it off, you inevitably get to think: OH MY GOSH, I'M OMNIPOTENT. The devil it's in the details. Balancing rules can't help if nobody knows/uses them. Plus, you need to understand what's unbalanced and what's balanced to make these rules (and that means understanding the rules).<br /> <br /> My problem was always with penalizing the (already weak) improvized magick, without adressing the real problem that it's the Ritual abuse. That's why I applaud the harsher rules for Rituals found in M20, while hating the newer rules of Counterspelling.<br /> <br /> <br /> The trick to balance mages, I think, it's to adjust the successes needed. Anything worth more than 4 sucesses it's outside the realm of posibility for a starting mage to do in a turn. Anything worth more than 5 might require a long ritual, specialy with the new rules for rituals.<br /> Turning things into silver seems too easy at Matter 2 for our werebeasts?. Well, Silver it's a precious metal, precious metals are harder to do than normal metals. So, let's say, 3 successes for a single bullet seems fair (let's give mages an attack, at least). 4 may be required to turn things that aren't already metal. 5-6 to transmute the floor (it's an area of effect, it shouldn't be easier than that). Really sadistic and want to turn the very air into silver?. Fine, 8 successes-it's an area casting where you try to turn a gaseous element into a solid, that happens to be a precious metal, and I just don't fell compelled to make it easy...<br /> As you can see, a lot depends on the storyteller. By doing that, I can kill any pretence of omnipotence at the reach of a casting roll. If you cast during various turns (how did you managed to not get killed?), you may end casting the Air into Silver Rote...or not, if I decide that such amount requires a ritual casting (spanning minutes or hours, not turns). If you add extra counter-rules to regular casting, either mages will end being unable to do anything without rituals, or the Storyteller it's going to counter-balance those rules by making magick cost less successes...and rituals would be as OP as ever. <hr />Also, too much balancing ends souring the taste of the games. For instance, I see no one arguing to weaken werewolves in order to make them more compatible with starting characters of other splats...In fact, I think that would anger many. However, they are way more unbalanced than Mages as far as PvP goes. They can steamroll any combat oriented build, and if a mage can do anything about it, it's not without a difficult/long ritual.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-15T07:46:42-07:00","id":891149,"title":"","content":"I'm all for a &quot;One World of Darkness&quot; splat, but only within reason. <br /> <br /> What I'd want from such a book is two-fold: <br /> <br /> 1) Better adjudication of powers, as the OP pointed out. Too many abilities rely on splat-specific abilites to determine things like difficulty. CoD does this better, with its Resistance abilities and the fact the core supernatural stat is pretty much a &quot;resist other powers&quot; boost. While adding the former is a bit harder in WoD (*glares at Appearance*), it only takes a little tinkering to do the same with the latter. It's part of the reason I ported Blood Potency into Masquerade in my House Rules and tweaked it to play nicely with Generation.<br /> <br /> 2) How the various subspecies interact with one another. Yes, yes, I get it that everyone likes to keep to themselves, and I have no problem with that, but it's not always possible. Nor is it particularly realistic. Sure, Garou hate Kindred and pretty much have a Kill-on-Sight policy (boring, imo), but Mages and Garou share living space as it were, with Caerns/Nodes and the Umbra. Wouldn't Dreamspeakers at least have some contacts? Or what if a cabal of mages gets Technocrats on their tail and wind up getting themselves indebted to the local Prince in return for protection? I'm not saying every supernatural group needs to have a weekly luncheon where they all get together and trade legends, life stories, and phone numbers. But the groups should brush up against one another from time to time, and it'd be nice to have some guidelines on that beyond &quot;X doesn't care about Y so they don't know anything about them at all&quot; which is pretty much the official line since Day One.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3200-barachiel","name":"Barachiel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3200_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"221"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-15T11:08:36-07:00","id":891258,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Barachiel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/882675-4th-eddition-better-one-world-system?p=891149#post891149\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm all for a &quot;One World of Darkness&quot; splat, but only within reason.<br /> <br /> What I'd want from such a book is two-fold:<br /> <br /> 1) Better adjudication of powers, as the OP pointed out. Too many abilities rely on splat-specific abilites to determine things like difficulty. CoD does this better, with its Resistance abilities and the fact the core supernatural stat is pretty much a &quot;resist other powers&quot; boost. While adding the former is a bit harder in WoD (*glares at Appearance*), it only takes a little tinkering to do the same with the latter. It's part of the reason I ported Blood Potency into Masquerade in my House Rules and tweaked it to play nicely with Generation.</div> </div> </div> </div>Having a strict category for each Attribute forces too much symmetry on the operation of everything. Also, why do we need power stats?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> 2) How the various subspecies interact with one another. Yes, yes, I get it that everyone likes to keep to themselves, and I have no problem with that, but it's not always possible. Nor is it particularly realistic. Sure, Garou hate Kindred and pretty much have a Kill-on-Sight policy (boring, imo), </div> </div> </div>Admit it - if you could, as a vampire, eliminate other vampires so easily, you'd love it.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> but Mages and Garou share living space as it were, with Caerns/Nodes and the Umbra. Wouldn't Dreamspeakers at least have some contacts? </div> </div> </div>Maybe if the Dreamspeakers were actual shamans and not reality warpers. The former mean that Garou can, under the present setup, accept hedge magic practitioners, but won't let a mage with an avatar anywhere near the caern because it isn't &quot;just a node&quot; like just about any given mage thinks it is.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Or what if a cabal of mages gets Technocrats on their tail and wind up getting themselves indebted to the local Prince in return for protection? </div> </div> </div>That seems like it could happen already, should be even easier if you shift things around.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I'm not saying every supernatural group needs to have a weekly luncheon where they all get together and trade legends, life stories, and phone numbers. But the groups should brush up against one another from time to time, and it'd be nice to have some guidelines on that beyond &quot;X doesn't care about Y so they don't know anything about them at all&quot; which is pretty much the official line since Day One. </div> </div> </div>You're probably wanting a less antagonistic setup too, right? Because the splatbooks generally do have them rubbing up against each other, but that just makes, say, the Mokole hate vampires even more.<br /> <br /> (Also, have we talked about how stupid Kindred getting benefits from drinking the blood of high Pure Breed Changers is? Because it's absolutely stupid, nonsensical, and in need of setting on fire.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-15T14:25:06-07:00","id":891370,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/882675-4th-eddition-better-one-world-system?p=891258#post891258\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Having a strict category for each Attribute forces too much symmetry on the operation of everything. Also, why do we need power stats?<br /> <br /> ...<br /> <br /> <br /> You're probably wanting a less antagonistic setup too, right? Because the splatbooks generally do have them rubbing up against each other, but that just makes, say, the Mokole hate vampires even more.<br /> <br /> (Also, have we talked about how stupid Kindred getting benefits from drinking the blood of high Pure Breed Changers is? Because it's absolutely stupid, nonsensical, and in need of setting on fire.)</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> We don't, per se, but it does make resolving certain supernatural conflicts easier. It's what I'm doing till WoD actually does something about it officially.<br /> <br /> Not necessarily less antagonism, but less &quot;kill on sight&quot;/&quot;avoid at all costs&quot; reactions. As written, this is how all supernatural communities treat each other, and quite frankly, I find it stupid. I've got no problem with werewolves and vampires being at war, or changelings avoiding the banality and stagnation of the undead. But Mage and Wraith have almost no excuse for not having some degree of interaction with damn near every other splat (yes, wraiths are dead, but damn near every subspecies has their take on necromancers and ghost whisperers). Demon and Vampire would also have little problem interacting. I personally loathe Apocalypse and prefer Forsaken for Werewolves as far as lore and purpose goes.<br /> <br /> I've always broken down the various WoD factions thus:<br /> <br /> Camarilla Vampires: Rulers of the City. Who you run afoul of when dealing with things on a local level.<br /> <br /> Anarchs/Caitiff: the rank and file just trying to get by. The guys you'd run into in biker bars and seedy clubs looking for a quick snack. Unless in a Free State.<br /> <br /> Unaligned Clans: The mercenaries of the night.<br /> <br /> Sabbat Vampires: The Monstrous Undead. For when you want just want vampire antagonists in your setting, unless running.<br /> <br /> &quot;Forsaken&quot; Garou: (in my cosmology, the tribes that try to get along with humanity), the hunters of the &quot;civilized&quot; wilds, close to and even within cities.<br /> <br /> &quot;Pure&quot; Garou: (the Garou who want to purge humanity and generally hate everyone not them): Antagonists unless running a pure Werewolf game.<br /> <br /> Tradition Mages: Secretive, stand-off-ish, but a few will trade favors with those who need a working done.<br /> <br /> Technocratic Mages: The weird Men in Black guys and Cyborg Zombies who occassional show up when the Masquerade/Veil gets REALLY trashed. Most rank-in-file only think they're some kind of government agency. Those who've been around for a while fear these guys more than the Inquisition. The Ultimate Autumn People.<br /> <br /> Orphans: These are the ones most likely to wind up in debt to some vampire elder or sidhe noble, working as their own personal &quot;court mage&quot;. Of course, that usually gets the mage a drastically reduced life expectancy.<br /> <br /> Seelie Fae: Rarely encountered by any but mages, some childlings are nearly recruited as the Awakened before it's discovered how differently their gifts manifest. The more nature-oriented ones might make friends in the Were communities.<br /> <br /> Unseelie Fae: In areas where this Court holds power, there's usually some kind of truce (or state of cold war) with the local Kindred community. Most Fae of either court avoid vampires, except areas where Toreador or Malkavians hold domain.<br /> <br /> Wraiths: If you're a necromancer or ghost hunter, you pretty much run into these. Doesn't mean you know jack squat about what's going on on the other side of Veil, though.<br /> <br /> Fallen: Mages and Garou respond badly to these creatures, thinking them common demons. Vampires and even Changelings can find kinship with them, however. Though honestly, they're most likely looking for a new chesspiece in their schemes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3200,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3200-barachiel","user":"Barachiel","date":". 05-15-2016, 06:20 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3200-barachiel","name":"Barachiel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3200_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"221"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-15T17:19:40-07:00","id":891455,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Barachiel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/882675-4th-eddition-better-one-world-system?p=891370#post891370\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I personally loathe Apocalypse and prefer Forsaken for Werewolves as far as lore and purpose goes.</div> </div> </div> </div>Anything that involves putting ChroD into WoD is pretty much twice a pipe dream.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":23,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","user":"Saur Ops Specialist","date":". 05-15-2016, 09:24 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-15T20:04:29-07:00","id":891538,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/882675-4th-eddition-better-one-world-system?p=891455#post891455\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Anything that involves putting ChroD into WoD is pretty much twice a pipe dream.</div> </div> </div> </div>Only if you run with RAW and never customize anything, ever. <br /> <br /> I've gutted a good third of VtM and thanks to the Translation Guide, about 75% of Apocalypse for my own personal WoD.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3200-barachiel","name":"Barachiel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3200_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"221"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-15T20:57:52-07:00","id":891557,"title":"","content":"\u201cResisted by game-specific trait\u201d is something that needs to go, for the most part. When you say \u201cthe subject rolls Humanity\u201d and the subject is a werewolf or mage \u2014 or, arguably, even a human \u2014 you're forced to make up a solution. If resistance is always based on common traits such as attributes, you can always have a game-specific trait <i>supplement</i> the resistance; but you'll never have to question what trait to use. <br /> <br /> The exception to this is when the thing you're resisting is specific to your splat's nature. Only mages suffer from Paradox; so it's OK if Mage-specific traits are used to cope with it. Likewise, a vampire's Virtues are all abiut resisting urges that only vampires experience; so any powers that are resisted by vampiric Virtues are powers that <i>don't work</i> on non-vampires. <br /> <br /> That's the sort of thing I'm hoping to see in One World of Darkness and its sequel lines: not so much a setting that assumes that, say, vampires and mages will bump elbows all the time; but rather a rules system where when they <i>do</i> bump elbows, it will be blatantly obvious how to handle it. I also want the One World of Darkness core book to be about the mortals in the World of Darkness with some sort of generic Horrors system that gives you antagonists and plot fodder even if you don't own any other book.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-16T04:17:56-07:00","id":891664,"title":"","content":"&quot;You're forced to make up a solution&quot; is normal for the cWoD. I don't see how it's any different then adjudicating all the other weirdness that pops up. It was never designed as a &quot;proper&quot; system as it was a framework to let you fill in things to your liking. At times I wonder if it's a feature rather then a bug. Heck, nowaday 5E is taking a similar stance, and it's the best edition of D&amp;D yet.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-16T07:03:58-07:00","id":891708,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Asmodai</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/882675-4th-eddition-better-one-world-system?p=891664#post891664\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">\u201cYou're forced to make up a solution\u201d is normal for the cWoD.</div> </div> </div> </div>It has been; but I don't see that as a good thing. Note that I'm not talking about questions like \u201chow do Gifts interact with Disciplines?\u201d \u2014 more generally, \u201chow does game A's subsystem X interact with game B's subsystem Y?\u201d I'm asking for something much more modest than that: when writing <b>Vampire</b>, don't assume that everyone you'll be interacting with will have Vampire-specific traits. That's all. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Asmodai</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/882675-4th-eddition-better-one-world-system?p=891664#post891664\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't see how it's any different then adjudicating all the other weirdness that pops up. It was never designed as a \u201cproper\u201d system as it was a framework to let you fill in things to your liking. At times I wonder if it's a feature rather then a bug. Heck, nowaday 5E is taking a similar stance, and it's the best edition of D&amp;D yet.</div> </div> </div> </div>The point is that if you have a \u201cOne World of Darkness\u201d core and reference it whenever you're dealing with anything that might reasonably be applied to characters outside of your gameline, you can avoid the most egregious \u201cdo not play well together\u201d clashes for which the original World of Darkness gamelines were infamous. I'm not saying that OWoD should do things the same way that ChroD does (for instance, I'm not proposing that OWoD promote the notion of a semi-standardized \u201ctemplate\u201d); but ChroD illustrates the feasibility of such an approach.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-16T09:55:37-07:00","id":891821,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/882675-4th-eddition-better-one-world-system?p=891708#post891708\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It has been; but I don't see that as a good thing. Note that I'm not talking about questions like \u201chow do Gifts interact with Disciplines?\u201d \u2014 more generally, \u201chow does game A's subsystem X interact with game B's subsystem Y?\u201d I'm asking for something much more modest than that: when writing <b>Vampire</b>, don't assume that everyone you'll be interacting with will have Vampire-specific traits. That's all.<br /> <br /> The point is that if you have a \u201cOne World of Darkness\u201d core and reference it whenever you're dealing with anything that might reasonably be applied to characters outside of your gameline, you can avoid the most egregious \u201cdo not play well together\u201d clashes for which the original World of Darkness gamelines were infamous. I'm not saying that OWoD should do things the same way that ChroD does (for instance, I'm not proposing that OWoD promote the notion of a semi-standardized \u201ctemplate\u201d); but ChroD illustrates the feasibility of such an approach.</div> </div> </div> </div>I do get what you said, but in all my years of playing the game the bigger problem to crossover mechanics was the fluff then the odd cases when you need to wing an equivalency resistance<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-12T21:32:55-07:00","id":930709,"title":"","content":"I want vampires as vampires with vampire problems <br /> <br /> I want my werewolves to be werewolves with werewolf problems <br /> <br /> Etc<br /> <br /> <br /> Building things from the ground up to be interconnected muddies the themes between the games and sort of destroys the beauty of it all of you ask me. <br /> <br /> The game lines should semi reference each other as they do now but mainly have a hands off seperate world aproach. <br /> <br /> If you want to have a united world of darkness you have two options <br /> <br /> Kajigger the stuff to work together via homebrew <br /> <br /> Play chronicles of darkness as those game lines were made modular to actually fit together. Cwod has no need of this.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3837-slimjimjohnson","name":"Slimjimjohnson","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"135"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-14T16:17:53-07:00","id":931673,"title":"","content":"Different approaches, different tastes. I always liked the notion of a crossover-able 'one wod' better. Just makes more sense to me. IMO it doesn't stop the lines to have distinct themes and stories (or shouldn't be, I also want gothic-punk vampire, punk-transhumanist-mystical mage, etc. It would be a shame if, for example mage would lose some of the themes that make it good just tobe more vampire-ish in tones), but, in the end, I think it is absolutely doable.<br /> <br /> Moreover, I'm a little baffled about this whole absolutely separate lines thing. Most of the books I did read referenced to other supernaturals, novels featured other supernaturals. To me, fluff-wise, the wod is already 'one wod' and always was and it's time to make the rules more compatible with each other, therefore take away much of the headache the ST facing if want to do mixed chronicles. I don't even think that this necessiates one 'true' cosmology. People think and believe wildly different things all the time.<br /> <br /> To me, the ideal wod is one, where the lines are existing in one world and potentially, but not necessarily effecting each other (thus make possibilities rather than restrictions - which is always good in my book), while the separate lines still focusing on their own themes. Vampires do vampire things, mostly interacting with vampires, BUT if I want a gang-war between the local Bonegnawers and Gangrel, or the prince having some misguided mage lackeys as his ace-in-the hole, I want to do that also and with the full support of the rules.<br /> <br /> Maybe, it's CofD-ish, but I admit that part is one i always appreciated in CofD.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>If nothing worked, then let's think!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6363-pm\u00e1rk","name":"PM\u00e1rk","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6363_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2363"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-16T12:44:24-07:00","id":932597,"title":"","content":"It's simple, we need a comparable set of traits for powers, since this seems to be the common theme. Let's steal from CoD and make them a trinity of power/finesse/resistance. They can be tacked onto the back of any existing character sheet without faffing with unique traits. <br /> <br /> We'll call them what they are: Power, Finesse and Resistance. All we need then is a set of formulae to translate disparate unique traits into a set of three universal ones. <br /> <br /> Any suggestions? I'm thinking, for example, that Power for Vampires would take into consideration Generation and age (maybe add +1 for every 1,000 years of undeath). Finesse would be calculated from highest Discipline and, say, the number of high level Disciplines possessed. Resistance would be calculated from Self-control and the higher of Occult or Thaumaturgical Countermagic.<br /> <br /> Let's say every one of these traits is on a 1-10 scale and is rolled as a dice pool like Willpower. Use a combat-style system of opposed rolls. Simple. Alternatively, you could have them on a 1-5 scale (halve the numbers after adding them) and pair them with an appropriate Discipline (e.g., Resistance + Dominate to resist Mind).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-18T03:15:57-07:00","id":933331,"title":"","content":"What I'd like to have in a 4th Edition<ul><li>A CoD-style book for World Description and basic rules.</li> <li>Attributes akin to CoD</li> <li>The integrity system and the condition should make a transition from CoD</li> <li>Difficulties should, after all modifiers are calculated in, be between 5 and 9. Every modifier above 9 should be a success threshold, every modifier under 5 should be an automatic success.</li> <li>Powers (disciplines, gifts, etc) should grant additional dice, ususally and difficulty adjustment rarely.</li> <li>Damage, should be a fixed value - reducing the number of rolls for each combat action to: Attack and Soak (defensive action, if targeted character spends an action for that).</li> <li>Merit and Flaws being characteristics that are unlikely to change (gained, or lost). Make foreign languages learned a background, for Christ's sake.</li> <li>Anchors and Aspirations, or a similar system should be carried over from CoD, or Wraith's Pathos system</li> <li>Social Combat (and possibly mental combat) as seen in ASOIAF-RPG (or CoD, as I read in the wika)</li> </ul><br /> <br /> What I don't want to have in a 4th edition<ul><li>Rules and mechanics to have crossover. Being a mummy amongst Vampires or a Gurahl amongst Garou isn't a merit. I can see how this is suitable to regulate 100 people LARP organisations, but it has nothing to offer in a tabletop game.</li> <li>Every game should be it's own Setting. There is really no need to unify the games to make them more cross over friendly. And there is no need to regulate how the sewers are shared. Mutual agreement, uneasy stalemate, enforced decision by powerful individuals should all be okay, should not be defined any where.</li> <li>No streamlining of powers. Certainly there should be some clean-up regarding powers of disciplines/gifts that are somewhat similar, just because authors had similar ideas and created powers that are kind-of alike. But gifts should be their own thing, and not be redesigned to match disciplines of certain levels and so on.</li> <li>EDIT: Additional actions in a turn as a power. V20 Dark Ages, that made Celerity affect the normal multiple actions rules, seems to be the most balanced approach to Celerity so far. It should be ported to all game lines. Acton more than once in any given turn is unbalanced in a way that just can't be corrected in any easy way. So, just don't to it.</li> </ul><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1008,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1008-heinrich","user":"heinrich","date":". 07-18-2016, 06:20 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1008-heinrich","name":"heinrich","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1008_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-19T11:56:30-07:00","id":933999,"title":"","content":"The problem with the crossover is that not every splat uses power statistics. Garou have Gnosis, Changelings have Glamour, Mages have Arete, etc, but Wraiths and Vampires have nothing. I think that when the powers of two splats interact, it should be a reflexive contested roll, level of attacker power against level of defender power, with a difficulty equal to (level of opponent's power/2, rounded up, plus 5), with the power with the most successes gaining dominance (a tie would alert both participants that something is happening and would require a full reflexive contested roll of applicable Attribute plus applicable Ability). The exception would be powers that have specific rules governing interactions with the powers of other splats (see Mind Shields of Psychic Numina and Counterspells of Sorcery). In the case of the suggested rules, a vampire with Dominate 5 trying to attack a Garou with a specific level 3 Gift that gives immunity to mind control, would gain 5 dice and roll against difficulty 7 while the Garou would gain 3 dice and roll against difficulty 8. While the vampire will probably win, the Garou at least has a chance of resisting.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11683,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","user":"Aya Tari","date":". 07-19-2016, 02:59 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}